Certainly! Below is a simple C# program that prints "Hello, World!" to the console:

```csharp
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
- `using System;`: This directive is used to include the `System` namespace, which contains the `Console` class.
- `class Program`: This defines a class named `Program`. In C#, every program must have at least one class.
- `static void Main()`: This is the entry point of the program. The `Main` method is where the program starts executing.
- `Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");`: This line prints the string "Hello, World!" to the console.

To run this program, you can use a C# compiler or an integrated development environment (IDE) like Visual Studio or Visual Studio Code.
